//  PETPORTS -- DEFRAGMENTATION MODULE
//
//  THE FIRST MODULE THAT UNLOCKS WORK THE PORT USED TO DO FOR FREE.
//
//  Oblivious suppresses dispatch, medic and farming each ADD a task. This one
//  takes three generators that already existed and shipped ungated -- tidy,
//  compact and defrag -- and puts them behind something the player has to go
//  and find. That is deliberate, and it is the whole argument for the module
//  existing rather than the behaviour simply being on:
//
//    Fragmentation is the player's problem to care about or to ignore. A pet
//    that can be TOLD to fix it is worth something; a pet that always did it
//    quietly was worth nothing anyone could point at.
//
//  THREE BOXES UNDER ONE MODULE, and they are three halves of one job:
//
//      tidy       move what is in the wrong crate
//      compact    merge what is split inside one crate
//      defrag     gather what is spread across several
//
//  Each keeps its own checkbox for the reason dd.bubble.cargotoggle gives --
//  wanting one without the others is a reasonable thing to want, and a player
//  who likes their stragglers where they are should be able to say so. They
//  live on petData.toggles and are read through petportParticipates, so they
//  travel with the pet to another port exactly as the medic classes and the
//  farming activities do.
//
//  RESTOCKING IS NOT HERE, AND IT USED TO SHARE A BOX WITH TIDYING. It is the
//  second half of the deposit beacon -- a crate the player named an item and an
//  amount for -- and gating a thing somebody explicitly asked for behind a
//  module they may not own reads as the mod being broken. It kept its own
//  switch, ungated and defaulted on.
//
//  IT NEEDS NO petports_moduleEffects. Nothing about this changes the unit: it
//  changes what the PORT is willing to dispatch, which is the same channel
//  Oblivious and Medic use and nothing else.
//
//  BOTH HALVES COUNT TOWARD MAXWELL. Tidying and defragmenting are the two
//  directions of one goal -- reducing the work a player has to do to find
//  something -- and the achievement counts them together.

{
	"itemName" : "petports_module_defrag",
	"price" : 1000,
	"rarity" : "Rare",

	//  Shared with the other modules, so the categories.config.patch label and
	//  the petports_filtergroups.config subgroup that already exist cover this
	//  item too. A new category would need both added or it sorts to Unsorted.
	"category" : "petports_module",

	//  ART PENDING. The file does not exist yet; a missing icon renders as a
	//  placeholder box rather than failing the load, so this is testable
	//  without it.
	"inventoryIcon" : "petports_module_defrag.png",

	"description" : "Equip a pet with this module and it will ^green;tidy, compact and consolidate^reset; the storage in its network, gathering scattered stacks of the same item into one place.",
	"shortdescription" : "Defragmentation Module",

	//  petports_no_upcycling KEEPS IT OUT OF THE CONVERTER, or a unit hauling
	//  surplus to an upcycler turns the player's modules into treats.
	"itemTags" : [ "petports", "petports_module", "petports_no_upcycling" ],

	//  MAXSTACK 1 IS A REQUIREMENT. The pane moves modules with
	//  player.swapSlotItem(), which returns the whole cursor stack; it refuses a
	//  stack rather than trusting this field, so a stackable module would be
	//  refused forever and look broken.
	"maxStack" : 1,

	"petports_moduleFlags" : [ "defrag" ]
}
